==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|playnly}}, {{m|enm|pleinly}}, {{m|enm|pleyneliche}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|plain|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpleɪnli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-plainly.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪnli|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[plain]] manner; [[simply]]; [[basically]].
#: {{ux|en|She decorated the room '''plainly''' but neatly.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Johanna Spyri
|by=Eileen Hall
|title=Heidi
|year=1956
|origyear=1880
|page=95
|passage='Tell me '''plainly''' what you think of my daughter's little companion.'}}
# [[obviously|Obviously]]; [[clearly]].
#: {{ux|en|You will see that ours is '''plainly''' the better method.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=The stories did not seem to me to touch life. They were '''plainly''' intended to have a bracing moral effect, and perhaps had this result for the people at whom they were aimed. They left me with the impression of a well-delivered stereopticon lecture, with characters about as life-like as the shadows on the screen, and whisking on and off, at the mercy of the operator.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1932|year_published=1965|author=w:Delos W. Lovelace|title=[[w:King Kong (1933 film)|King Kong]]|page=3|passage='''Plainly''' he was prepared to bark out an interminable succession of charges against the Wanderer.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|obviously|clearly}} {{l|en|expressly}}, {{l|en|unambiguously}}; see also [[Thesaurus:explicitly]] or [[Thesaurus:obviously]]

